Grown Ups 2 is a 2013 American comedy film directed by Dennis Dugan, written by Adam
Sandler, Fred Wolf, and Tim Herlihy, and produced by Sandler and Jack Giarraputo.

12
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:42,000
It serves as a sequel to the 2010 film Grown Ups and features Sandler, Kevin James, Chris Rock, David Spade, Salma Hayek, Maya Rudolph, Maria
Bello, and most of the cast members reprising their roles from the first film, alongside Nick Swardson, who joins the cast.

13
01:05:39,000 --> 01:05:45,000
Lenny (played by Sandler) moves his family back to his
hometown, where he reunites with his old friends.

14
01:10:42,000 --> 01:10:48,000
Together, they face bizarre situations and new
enemies in the form of a local fraternity.

15
01:15:45,000 --> 01:15:51,000
Produced by Sandler's production company Happy Madison Productions and distributed by Sony Pictures
Releasing through its Columbia Pictures label, Grown Ups 2 was released on July 12, 2013.

16
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:54,000
It was panned by critics but grossed $247 million on an $80 million budget.

17
01:25:51,000 --> 01:25:57,000
It was nominated for nine Razzies at the 2014 Golden Raspberry Awards.

18
01:30:54,000 --> 01:31:00,000
The film explores themes of friendship, journey
in the past, cliff, past, sequel.

